    "note": "# AuraGraph Study Notes\n\n*Proficiency: **Beginner** — Conceptual focus — core ideas, zero math*\n\n> ⚠️ **Note:** These notes are generated using the `local_summarizer` fallback engine. Add your Azure OpenAI keys to `backend/.env` for true AI-fused notes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Let Xbe A Random Variable Such That\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** 1ifω=success 0ifω=failure Let the success probability denoted by pand failure probability by q= 1−pwith 0< p < 1.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** Write the definition first, then explain with an example for full marks.\n\n---\n\n## The Pmf Of Xis Defined As\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** If Xfollows the above PMF, we say Xfollows Bernoulli distribution and denote it by X∼Ber(p).\n\n💡 **Intuition:** Moment generating function. =q+pet 4 Binomial Distribution Idea.\n\nConsider nindependent and identical Bernoulli trials each with success probability p.\n\nLet Xbe a random variable denoting the number of success.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** Write the definition first, then explain with an example for full marks.\n\n---\n\n## Csl-373: Probability Theory For Computer Engineers\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** 1 Geometric Distribution Idea.\n\n💡 **Intuition:** Consider independent and identical (IID) Bernoulli trials (each with success probability p,0< p < 1) till the first success is achieved.\n\nLet Xbe a random variable denoting the number of trials needed for the first success.\n\nThen Xtakes values 1,2,···\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** Write the definition first, then explain with an example for full marks.\n\n---\n\n## The Pmf Of Xis Given By\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** If Xhas the above PMF, we say Xfollows Geometric distribution and denote it by X∼Geo(p).\n\n💡 **Intuition:** Show that V ar(X) =q p2.\n\nMoment generating function. i=1eitqi−1p =pet∞X =pet Memoryless property of Geometric distribution.\n\nStarting point does not matter in Geometric distribution.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** State the theorem/definition precisely — examiners award marks for exact wording.\n\n---\n\n## We