function. 0etuλe−λtdt 0e−t(λ−u)dt 0e−zdz λ−usetting t(λ−u) =z λ−uZ∞ 0e−zdz λ−u,foru < λ Memoryless property of Exponential distribution.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** State the theorem/definition precisely — examiners award marks for exact wording.\n\n---\n\n## Thus,\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** 1.4 Function of a random variable: Continuous case Let Xbe a continuous random variable defined over (Ω,F,P).\n\n💡 **Intuition:** Let Xbe a continuous random variable over (Ω,F,P).\n\nSuppose f(x)is a strictly monotonic (increasing or decreasing), differentiable (and thus continuous) function of x.\n\nThen the random variable Y defined by Y=f(X)has a probability density function given by fX(f−1(y))\f\f\f\fdf−1(y) 0, o.w.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** State the theorem/definition precisely — examiners award marks for exact wording.\n\n---\n\n## Differentiation Gives\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** Let Xbe a continuous random variable defined by 1,0< x < 1 0, o.w. λln(1−X)forλ > 0.\n\n💡 **Intuition:** Also, it is strictly increasing and differentiable.\n\nSo Theorem 3 can be applied to compute the PDF of Y. fX(f−1(y))\f\f\f\fdf−1(y) 0, o.w. 1.\f\f\f\fd(1−e−λy) 0, o.w. λe−λy,0< y < ∞ 0, o.w.\n\nCorollary of Theorem 3.\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** State the theorem/definition precisely — examiners award marks for exact wording.\n\n---\n\n## And Statistics For Engineers *(Textbook)*\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** Soong State University of New York at Buffalo, Buffalo, New York, USA TLFeBOOK TLFeBOOK\n\n> 📝 **Exam Tip:** Write the definition first, then explain with an example for full marks.\n\n---\n\n## West Sussex Po19 8Sq, England *(Textbook)*\n\n🔰 **Core Concept:** Telephone ( 44) 1243 779777 Email (for orders and customer service enquiries): cs-books@wiley.co.uk Visit our Home Page on www.wileye urope.com or www.wiley.com All Rights Reserved.\n\n💡 **Intuition:** No part of this publication may be reproduced, stored in a retrievalsystem or transmitted in any form or by any means, electronic, mechanical, photocopying, 